  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: Three experiments establish that RNA is the dominant modality (~48-52% vs ~21% for image) and that the learned scvi_n200 encoder outperforms PCA-2000 by ~3.5 points in the single-profile setting. However, all experiments so far are single-profile; the effect of multiprofile aggregation is completely untested. Uncertainty: It is unknown whether aggregating multiple profiles (via avgpool) adds meaningful signal beyond a single profile, and whether the encoder advantage of scvi_n200 compounds or diminishes under aggregation. This experiment (config_005: rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) tests the single design decision of adding multiprofile + avgpool on top of the best-known RNA encoder, directly comparable to config_004. If it yields a substantial gain over 52%, aggregation is a key axis to exploit; if the gain is marginal, it tells us the single-profile RNA signal is near its ceiling and we should pivot to testing fusion or alternative encoders. This is the highest-information next step because it resolves the most critical unexplored axis (profile/aggregation) while keeping the encoder at its best-validated setting, and it uses the simpler avgpool before committing to the more complex transformer."
}

